# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleUSM14 = M14
    .desc = The M14 was kindof a flop, it tried to be an infantry rifle, a machinegun, and a sniper all at once. It was meh at the first and decent enough at the third to stick around with national guard or police armouries and some designated marksmen in the proper army.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleBESCARL = SCAR-L
    .desc = Meant to replace the M4A1 in US service, but lost the bid and was overshadowed by the SCAR-H. Still sees service in belgium. Takes STANAG magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleBESCARH = SCAR-H
    .desc = The big brother of the SCAR-L, not entirely replacing the M4A1 but select units can choose to take a few. Takes SCAR-H pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleBEFAL = FN FAL
    .desc = The right arm of the free world, would've fired an intermediate cartridge and been the standard service rifle of NATO if it weren't for America, and maybe Germany. Takes FAL pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleBEFALPara = FAL PARA
    .desc = A cut down FAL with a ~16 inch barrel and folding stock, for paratroopers. Takes FAL pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG27K = G27K
    .desc = A full auto 417 with a factory short barrel for dirty work up close.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG3A3 = G3A3
    .desc = Derived from the spanish CETME rifle, think of this weapon as the MP5's older brother who does steroids. Was used by west germany post WW2 until it was replaced by the G36 after reunification. Takes G3 pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG3A4 = G3A4
    .desc = A G3 variant with a collapsable stock and darker furniture. A neat package but you won't be stuffing it in your bag. Takes G3 pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG3A3ZF = G3A3ZF
    .desc = A G3A3 with a ZF1 scope mounted. Used by sharpshooters and soldiers alike. At least 60 years ago. Takes G3 pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG36K = G36K
    .desc = Plastic fantastic, or plastich fantastich if you're german.. or deutsch. Takes G36 pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG36 = G36
    .desc = Plastic fantastic, or plastich fantastich if you're german.. or deutsch. Takes G36 pattern magazines.

# Resources\Prototypes\_Battlefield14\Entities\Objects\Weapons\Guns\Rifles\rifles.yml
ent-BF14WeaponRifleDEG36C = G36C
    .desc = Plastic fantastic, or plastich fantastich if you're german.. or deutsch. Takes G36 pattern magazines.

